"Morveth cuidaba el jardín de un hospital sitiado. Cuando las medicinas se agotaron, descubrió un micelio capaz de retener la infección en sus raíces. Ahora transporta aquel cultivo en una urna agrietada. Sus hongos necesitan tiempo y terreno para extenderse; arrancarlos deja al jardinero expuesto. No busca una cura perfecta, sino impedir que la próxima cosecha sean los vivos.": "Morveth tended the garden of a besieged hospital. When the medicine ran out, he discovered a mycelium able to hold the infection in its roots. Now he carries that culture in a cracked urn. His fungi need time and ground to spread; tearing them out leaves the gardener exposed. He doesn't seek a perfect cure, but to keep the next harvest from being the living.",
